==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|Maffia||less common}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|it|Mafia}}. Perhaps from {{der|en|it|mafia||spirit of hostility to the law}} or from {{der|en|scn|mafiusu||boldness, bravado}}. See [[w:Mafia|the Wikipedia article]] for more discussion of the origin of the word.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈmɑfi.ə/}}
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈmæfi.ə/}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|head=the Mafia}}

# {{senseid|en|Mob}} The {{l|en|Mob}}: any particular [[mafia]], mentioned uniquely within the discussion's established or implicit context, usually and especially the Sicilian–Italian–Italian-American one (especially in American English) but occasionally others (e.g., the Russian one, the Japanese one).
#: {{syn|en|Mob}}
## The international [[criminal]] organization of [[Sicilian]] origin operating in [[Italy]] and the [[United States]].
##: {{syn|en|Cosa Nostra}}
## Any other specific organized crime [[syndicate]] operating internationally in high-level [[organized crime]]; {{non-gloss definition|often with a modifying adjective, such as a nationality}}.
##: {{ux|en|Somehow he managed to upset the Russian '''Mafia'''.}}
# A [[party game]] modelling a [[conflict]] between an informed [[minority]] (the mafia) and an uninformed [[majority]] (the innocents). Each player is secretly assigned a role within one of these teams, and the innocents attempt to identify the mafia members before they are all "murdered".

